#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:58
msgid "INITIAL DATASET"
msgstr "CONJUNTO DE DATOS INICIAL"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:59
msgid ""
"Create an initial JSON or CSV dataset to be used as the collection for "
"this option list. It should be a list containing objects with properties "
"'name' and 'value'"
msgstr "Cree un conjunto de datos inicial JSON o CSV para usar como la colección de esta lista de opciones. Debe ser una lista que contenga objetos con las propiedades 'name' y 'value'"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:69
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:325
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:445
msgid "TRANSLATION SCRIPT"
msgstr "SCRIPT DE TRADUCCIÓN"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:61
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:128
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:445
msgid ""
"Create a JS script to translate the result data object into an array "
"containing objects with properties 'name' and 'value'. The input data is "
"provided as 'data' and the result should be put on the global variable "
"'results'."
msgstr "Cree un script JS para traducir el objeto de datos del resultado en un arreglo que contenga objetos con las propiedades 'name' y 'value'. Los datos de entrada se proporcionan como 'data' y el resultado debe colocarse en la variable global 'results'."

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:63
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:74
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:130
msgid "**Example:**"
msgstr "**Ejemplo:**"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:65
msgid ""
"for(var x=0;x < data.length; x++) {\n"
"  results.push({name: data[x].name,value:data[x].id});\n"
"}"
msgstr "for(var x=0;x < data.length; x++) {\\n  results.push({name: data[x].name,value:data[x].id});\\n}"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:121
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:431
msgid "REQUEST SCRIPT"
msgstr "SCRIPT DE SOLICITUD"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:72
msgid ""
"Create a JS script to prepare the request. Return a data object as the "
"body for a POST request, and return an array containing properties 'name'"
" and 'value' for a GET request. The input data is provided as 'data' and "
"the result should be put on the global variable 'results'"
msgstr "Cree un script JS para preparar la solicitud. Devuelva un objeto de datos como el cuerpo para una solicitud POST, y devuelva un arreglo que contenga propiedades 'name' y 'value' para una solicitud GET. Los datos de entrada se proporcionan como 'data' y el resultado debe colocarse en la variable global 'results'"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:76
#, python-brace-format
msgid "results.push({name: 'userId', value : data.users})"
msgstr "results.push({name: 'userId', value : data.users})"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:80
msgid ""
"In a GET request (SOURCE METHOD = GET), the value of the results variable"
" is used to build out the request parameters. Thus, in the example "
"``results`` value:"
msgstr "In a GET request (SOURCE METHOD = GET), the value of the results variable se usa para build out the request parameters. Thus, in the example ``results`` value:"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:82
#, python-brace-format
msgid "results=[{name:\"name1\",value: \"value1\"}]"
msgstr "results=[{name:\\\"name1\\\",value: \\\"value1\\\"}]"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:86
msgid "The request would be made to: ``https://<someURL>?name1=value1``."
msgstr "La solicitud se realizaría a: ``https://<someURL>?name1=value1``."

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:88
msgid ""
"In a POST request (SOURCE METHOD = POST), the value of the results "
"variable is used to build the body of the POST request. Thus, in the "
"example ``results`` value:"
msgstr "In a POST request (SOURCE METHOD = POST), the value of the results variable se usa para build the body of the POST request. Thus, in the example ``results`` value:"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:90
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"results=[{name:\"name1\", value:\"value1\"}, {name:\"name2\", "
"value:\"value2\"}]"
msgstr "results=[{name:\\\"name1\\\", value:\\\"value1\\\"}, {name:\\\"name2\\\", value:\\\"value2\\\"}]"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:94
#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:116
msgid "The following JSON body would be posted to the target URL:"
msgstr "El siguiente cuerpo JSON se enviaría al URL de destino:"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:96
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{name:\"name1\", value:\"value1\"}, {name:\"name2\", value:\"value2\"}"
msgstr "{name:\\\"name1\\\", value:\\\"value1\\\"}, {name:\\\"name2\\\", value:\\\"value2\\\"}"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:100
msgid ""
"An alternative method to building the POST request (SOURCE METHOD = "
"POST), can be seen below.  As well, we can access other **Inputs** that "
"are available on the same form, when provisioning an Instance or Catalog "
"Item. As seen below, the other Inputs can be accessed using the ``data`` "
"variable.  We can access another Input by calling its **Field Name**, "
"which can be configured when editing the Input in |LibOptInp|.  This "
"allows using data from other Inputs to be used in this Input's request."
msgstr "An alternative method to building the POST request (SOURCE METHOD = POST), can be seen below.  As well, we can access other **Inputs** that are available on the same form, when provisioning an Instancia or Catalog Item. As seen below, the other Inputs can be accessed using the ``data`` variable.  We can access another Input by calling its **Field Name**, which puede ser configured when editing the Input in |LibOptInp|.  This allows using data from other Inputs to be used in this Input's request."

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:104
msgid ""
"In the example below the Input Field Name we'll access is "
"``myinputfieldname``, which we can get either the name (visible value for"
" lists) or value from the item:"
msgstr "In el/la example abajo el/la Input Field Name we'll access es ``myinputfieldname``, el/la cual we puede/n get either el/la name (visible value para lists) o value desde el/la item:"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:106
msgid ""
"Name variable:  ``data.myinputfieldname`` Value variable:  "
"``data.myinputfieldname_value``"
msgstr "Name variable:  ``data.myinputfieldname`` Value variable:  ``data.myinputfieldname_value``"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:109
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"var postBody = {};\n"
"postBody[\"number\"] = data.myinputfieldname_value;\n"
"postBody[\"env\"] = \"all\";\n"
"results = postBody;"
msgstr "var postBody = {};\\npostBody[\\\"number\\\"] = data.myinputfieldname_value;\\npostBody[\\\"env\\\"] = \\\"all\\\";\\nresults = postBody;"

#: ../../library/options/option_lists.rst:118
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{ \"number\": \"123456\", \"env\": \"all\" }"
msgstr "{ \\\"number\\\": \\\"123456\\\", \\\"env\\\": \\\"all\\\" }"

